# Kept out of the build context. The Containerfile COPYs only image/,
# features/, installer/ and keys/cosign.pub; the Secure Boot key material
# enters via `podman build --secret`, never via the context.
#
# home/ and dotfiles.sh are listed first on purpose: the dotfiles are NOT part
# of any image and must never become part of one. Excluding them here means a
# stray COPY cannot even reach them.
home
dotfiles.sh

.git
.gitignore
.containerignore
output
docs
.github
**/*.md
Justfile
renovate.json
# the dev container and the VS Code Flatpak, built from their own directory
devtools

# keys/ holds private key material (git-ignored *.key), so the whole directory
# stays out of the build context. The one exception is the cosign PUBLIC key:
# the image needs it to verify its own updates (/etc/containers/policy.json),
# and it is public by definition. Order matters, the negation must come after
# the directory it re-includes from.
keys
!keys/cosign.pub
